   "tags": "Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements in reference to transformation of stresses:<br />\n1. In case of two like and equal principal stresses, the resultant stress on any plane is equal to the principal stresses.<br />\n2. In case of two equal and unlike stresses, the resultant stress on any plane is equal to principal stresses.<br />\n3. In case of two like and equal principal stresses, the obliquity of the resultant stress is on any plane is zero.<br />\n4. In a strained material subjected to two dimensional stresses, the sum of normal stresses on any two mutually perpendicular planes is equal to the sum of major and minor principal stresses.<br />\nWhich of the above statements are correct?</p>",
